WEBVTT

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.790
<i>I'm glad I met you.</i>

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.350
I'm back.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.790
Welcome back!

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.000
Yeah, glad to be home.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.580
Welcome home.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.380
Did you bring me a present?

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.510
It's inside.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.520
Something else in a bottle?

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.130
It's beautiful!

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:47.070
How come Mom gets a pretty ring 
and I just got water in a bottle?

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.660
Your bottle's filled with 
dreams and adventure.

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.900
How much did it cost?

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.900
Um.. ten... ten gold pieces?

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:57.970
That's cheap!

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:01.360
What's important isn't the cost, 
it's the feelings behind it.

00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:05.370
Let's eat!

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:09.490
Sorry I'm not home more often.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:10.750
It's fine.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:15.340
How long will you be gone 
on your next journey?

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.170
My healer for this trip has a habit 
of changing their mind a lot.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:21.230
I'll probably be gone a long time.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.220
But I'll be back by winter.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.530
Winter?

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.250
Yeah.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:43.660
This is a good village.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:49.780
It's out here near the wilderness, but
monsters and humans live in peace together.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.560
But a long time ago,

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.500
monsters used to be things
 that only attacked people.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.750
Until the healers appeared.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.750
The healers have the power to 
heal the hearts of monsters.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.440
You have that power, too, you know.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:14.770
I've heard that a hundred times now.

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.620
I haven't told you that many times.

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:31.650
Dad...

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.550
Winter's almost over.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.320
A...

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:27.220
A girl?

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.320
<b>The Apathetic Boy and the Girl in a Bottle</b>

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:08.450
<b>The Apathetic Boy and the Girl in a Bottle</b>

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:23.580
Yuu-san?

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.530
It's me, Merc.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.540
Is there anything you can do about him?

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.720
Oh, fine.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:34.930
Um...

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.900
I'm sorry about Yuu-san.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.620
Thank you.

00:05:46.850 --> 00:05:48.960
It was a horrific battle.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:51.820
It seemed more like a hilarious battle to me.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.300
Or maybe a pathetic battle...

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.260
There's a lot of ways you could take it.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:56.720
What do you expect me to do?

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:58.560
If I'm scared, I'm scared!

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.780
I can't talk to them,

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.730
and I don't know what they're thinking.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:05.630
Even if they've been healed, I don't 
know when they'll turn on me—

00:06:07.480 --> 00:06:10.960
Are you going to buy anything, or just gawk?

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.710
Oh, I'm sorry. We're here to buy things.

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:16.170
We really want to buy things!

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.700
So sparkly! Look at the sparklies!

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.610
Yuu-san, let's make that our first purchase.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:29.610
No, we've got things we really 
need to buy for our trip.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.750
You two are going on a trip by yourselves?

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.080
Huh? Well...

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.960
I guess. Maybe... Maybe not...

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:40.130
We are!

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:40.910
Hey!

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:42.960
Are you sure?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.930
There are all kinds of 
unhealed monsters out there.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:48.120
Yeah, I know...

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:51.290
Merc, you heard the woman. 
Let's try this another time—

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:52.850
It has to be today!

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:58.430
My horoscope said it was the perfect day 
to leave on a journey to find yourself!

00:06:58.430 --> 00:07:04.500
You're more interested in what it said about 
meeting a handsome knight, aren't you?

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:08.610
Forget it.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:11.140
Love between a liquid and 
a solid never works.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:14.280
You won't know that for 
sure until I fall in love!

00:07:13.040 --> 00:07:14.880
She's a strange one...

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:15.410
It's not happening.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.360
Yeah.

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:20.880
I've never seen a girl who looks 
like a fairy in town before.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:24.040
Is she maybe some incredibly 
powerful magic-user?

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:28.340
You've got a sharp eye!

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:33.930
I'm actually the Magical Girl 
in a Bottle, and my job is

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:37.380
to heal hearts that are 
tired from long journeys!

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:42.260
See? Just looking at me makes 
you feel relaxed, doesn't it?

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:44.160
All you can do is float and tell bad jokes.

00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:47.410
So maybe you're the powerful one?

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.160
You've got a sharp eye.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:52.480
I'm actually...

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.220
...famous for being the biggest 
wimp in the village,

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.130
and for running away faster 
than anybody else!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.090
I know it's true, but you 
don't have to tell them that!

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.090
They're friends... right?

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.370
Yeah.

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:08.250
I guess I don't have any memories 
from before I met Yuu-san.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:13.740
So I was hoping I could go on a 
journey someday to get them back.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.420
I know that.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:16.830
But we need to prepare properly,

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.640
and not just do it because 
your horoscope said so.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:23.750
Kid, you don't need a real reason 
to set out on a journey.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.570
Why not go with a merchant caravan?

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:28.100
You'll be able to go to 
all kinds of countries.

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:33.120
You may be able to meet somebody 
who knows about that fairy girl.

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:36.390
And so...

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.880
Let's start you off with a 
Beginner's Traveling Set.

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.860
<i>She's in salesgirl mode now.</i>

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.310
<i>And she takes her job seriously.</i>

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.530
And this...

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:47.050
A stink bag to keep monsters away.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:48.620
Stink bag?

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.200
I recommend it.

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:54.230
If you carry it, it will keep monsters away.

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:55.540
Really?

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:59.180
There's still trouble with monsters 
in other countries, they say.

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:00.220
I'll buy it!

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.160
That was fast!

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:02.720
That'll be 5,000 gold pieces!

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.380
It's so pricey!

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:04.770
But I'll buy it anyway.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.230
Thanks for your purchase!

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.890
Yuu-san, does your allowance cover that?

00:09:08.890 --> 00:09:13.140
Actually, if you're going to waste money 
like that, then give me some sparklies!

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:16.480
I'll buy you something else next time.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:21.250
As long as I've got this, I don't 
need to be afraid of monsters.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.640
Wh-What was that?

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.910
A sentient fluffball?

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:36.330
No, it was a monster.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:39.030
It was definitely a monster.

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:44.690
Let's follow it!

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:46.890
Thank you!

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:50.890
Wait, Merc!

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:01.040
Wait! That's the money for my sparkly ring!

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.370
I told you, I'm not buying 
you any sparklies!

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:08.930
Forget that, if a monster 
carries a stink bag...

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:13.240
Something awful might 
happen to that fluffball!

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:16.130
We need to catch it now!

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:26.810
It fell?!

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:31.610
A monster?!

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:34.430
Come one, come all!

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:36.660
The carnival's in town!

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:38.960
And today's the last day!

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:43.540
It's a monster carnival.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:46.710
Wait!

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:48.420
Wait...

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:50.830
Wait!

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:55.850
Mr. Fluffy, calm down.

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.800
Start by giving me that bag...

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:06.130
So... fluffy...

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.930
Yuu-san?

00:11:13.930 --> 00:11:15.980
That was close...

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:19.270
Don't run off on your own.

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:22.180
We don't know what will happen 
if the bottle breaks.

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:24.000
Sorry.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:28.100
Well, thanks to that, we got
 our stink bag back...

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:33.160
Oh, no!

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.530
What happened?

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:44.170
Mr. Flambear looks really mad.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:48.350
The tiny floof came 
bouncing out, and, um...

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.140
It wrecked the tent!

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:58.520
Yuu-san, use your healing magic!

00:11:58.520 --> 00:11:59.860
Healing magic?

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:00.600
Magic?

00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:02.430
Healing magic?

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:05.200
You're a healer?

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.360
What are you doing here?!

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:07.790
We're saved!

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:10.400
Heal that Flambear, now!

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.680
No, um...

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:14.980
I can't really...

00:12:13.780 --> 00:12:16.330
Go for it! Blast the thing!

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.880
You can do it!

00:12:23.850 --> 00:12:26.690
Please save us!

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:34.850
<b>The Apathetic Boy and the Girl in a Bottle</b>

00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:45.850
Nobody's following me anymore, right?

00:12:45.850 --> 00:12:50.040
Yuu-san, I'm sorry about that.

00:12:50.470 --> 00:12:55.530
You got so nervous that 
you couldn't even try it.

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:58.570
Sorry!

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:00.170
I was wrong to say anything...

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:05.860
Well, even if I wasn't nervous, it still
 probably wouldn't have worked.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:10.920
Anyway...

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:13.290
Mr. Fluffball!

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.360
Just forget it.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:18.530
I'm talking about this!

00:13:20.120 --> 00:13:23.100
It's really bothering me!

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:24.640
What is?

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:32.360
Mr. Fluffball was weakened 
after he stole the stink bag.

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:35.410
There must be some reason he did it.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:38.190
Who cares if there was?

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:40.490
You're sure about that?

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:41.630
Stop it!

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:44.040
It's not our problem.

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:47.520
He vanished during all 
that commotion, right?

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:49.620
He was probably just messing around.

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.610
He's probably out there having a 
fluffing good time somewhere.

00:13:58.190 --> 00:13:59.930
Fine.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:04.360
What was that?

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:08.050
It came from the forest!

00:14:19.360 --> 00:14:21.010
What happened?!

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:34.410
Ow...

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.080
You okay, Merc?

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.530
Yeah.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:45.330
It's an Enigma!

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:48.570
An unhealed... monster?!

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:56.070
Mr. Fluffball protected you!

00:14:56.070 --> 00:14:56.940
No way...

00:14:56.940 --> 00:14:59.060
You okay?

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:15.580
Why is it coming after me?

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:21.280
The book said that unhealed 
monsters attack humans!

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:22.530
Why?

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.640
Nobody knows!

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.630
Mr. Fluffball!

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.420
Yuu-san, ahead of you!

00:15:39.520 --> 00:15:40.650
Oh, no!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:57.290
It's trying to save me?

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:12.040
Yuu-san!

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:34.000
Yuu-san, now!

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:35.920
Use your healing magic!

00:17:52.890 --> 00:17:56.200
It looks so peaceful now.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:00.240
You healed it!

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:06.010
Yeah...

00:18:07.250 --> 00:18:11.630
<i>The healers have the power to 
heal the hearts of monsters.</i>

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:13.430
<i>You have that power, too, you know.</i>

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:28.030
It's going to take a little more time 
for you to get used to monsters, huh?

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:31.070
Stay away!

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:32.660
Get away!

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.810
I solved the mystery!

00:18:43.340 --> 00:18:48.800
Mr. Fluffy was trying to keep his friend, 
Mr. Enigma, away from the city...

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:51.210
Who's "Mr. Fluffy"?

00:18:51.210 --> 00:18:53.950
It's the name of that fluffy monster!

00:18:53.950 --> 00:18:55.500
That's a terrible name.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.950
That doesn't matter right now!

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:04.340
What matters is that Mr. Fluffy wanted 
to get that stink bag to help his friend,

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.820
who hadn't been properly healed.

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:11.610
Unhealed monsters attack 
any people they see.

00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:16.210
Mr. Fluffy didn't want his 
friend to attack humans.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:20.280
So that's the story, huh?

00:19:20.280 --> 00:19:22.610
The two of them were friends, huh?

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:24.050
That's right!

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:29.010
Monsters have hearts and care about 
their friends, just like humans!

00:19:29.010 --> 00:19:31.810
How did you figure that out, anyway?

00:19:31.810 --> 00:19:34.120
I asked Mr. Fluffy!

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:39.380
I left all the things you'll 
need for your journey

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.860
with Jamo-san, the man 
you'll be traveling with.

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:43.710
Thank you.

00:19:43.710 --> 00:19:44.580
How much do I owe—

00:19:44.580 --> 00:19:45.360
Nothing.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.960
This is our way of thanking you for
 healing the monster in the forest.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:51.870
No, but I didn't mean to...

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.870
Even if you didn't mean to,

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:57.880
you stopped a fight before it started.

00:19:58.380 --> 00:19:59.990
Without a healer to help us,

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.950
the only thing we can do with 
monsters is fight them.

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:05.620
Hey!

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:09.390
It's time to go, jamo!

00:20:10.530 --> 00:20:11.880
Have a nice journey!

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.280
Thanks!

00:20:33.090 --> 00:20:37.540
It's great that we were able to get 
a job guarding Jamo-san's carriage.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.160
Yeah.

00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.890
Come on, lighten up!

00:20:42.890 --> 00:20:45.140
This isn't a vacation!

00:20:45.140 --> 00:20:46.630
Jamo-san! Jamo-san!

00:20:47.940 --> 00:20:50.350
Where are we going?

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.990
Let me see, jamo.

00:20:53.990 --> 00:20:58.040
The world of Meftelharne is a big one...

00:20:58.800 --> 00:21:04.330
Well, we're going to a place where 
we can make a ton of money!

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.910
I can't wait.

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.460
Yeah, but where is that?

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:16.280
That's him...

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.490
It's so beautiful!

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:38.880
It wants to come with us!

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:42.350
Glad to have you along!

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:46.510
I'm not! Get off me!

00:23:25.690 --> 00:23:27.000
I'm Titi!

00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:27.960
I'm Chacha!

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:30.820
The <i>Merc Storia</i> anime has finally begun!

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:34.560
Me and my sister will do the 
best we can to promote it!

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:37.780
Next time: "The King of Dawn 
and the Imprisoned Bride."

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>The King of Dawn and the Imprisoned Bride</b>

00:23:37.780 --> 00:23:40.200
Look forward to it!
